WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.667
Cooking odors travel with kitchen exhaust.

00:00:03.027 --> 00:00:06.147
The Molitron Odor
Abatement System, or MOAS,

00:00:06.447 --> 00:00:10.247
uses a treatment mist inside the
duct to help control those odors.

00:00:10.747 --> 00:00:12.487
Here's what to plan for your restaurant.

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:18.823
The wall-mounted MOAS cabinet
weighs about 100 pounds

00:00:18.833 --> 00:00:22.413
and connects to a separate
10-gallon solution reservoir.

00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:24.563
Plan suitable wall support

00:00:24.573 --> 00:00:26.933
and a location staff can check easily.

00:00:27.853 --> 00:00:30.753
The low-solution alarm needs
to be heard from the kitchen.

00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:33.293
Keep the reservoir easy to reach,

00:00:33.593 --> 00:00:35.513
with room for staff to add solution.

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.720
The MOAS connects to your building's
electrical supply and cold water.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:42.870
We recommend an accessible
external water shutoff

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.040
so staff can shut off the supply
without opening the cabinet.

00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:48.720
There is also a shutoff inside the unit.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.660
A separate fan-on connection
enables power to the MOAS.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:57.347
Two lines run from the cabinet
toward the duct-mounted nozzles.

00:00:57.807 --> 00:01:01.607
The 3/8-inch black tubing
carries compressed air,

00:01:01.947 --> 00:01:04.997
while the 1/4-inch red
tubing carries solution

00:01:05.007 --> 00:01:06.507
already mixed with water.

00:01:07.347 --> 00:01:10.377
In this example, they follow
a supported conduit route

00:01:10.387 --> 00:01:12.507
before branching to both nozzles.

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:16.627
Vertical or horizontal nozzle
installations can be accommodated.

00:01:16.987 --> 00:01:19.377
This example uses a
horizontal configuration

00:01:19.387 --> 00:01:21.167
on opposite sides of the duct.

00:01:22.547 --> 00:01:26.037
During operation, air and mixed
solution meet at the nozzles

00:01:26.047 --> 00:01:29.327
to create a fine mist, which
moves with the exhaust airflow.

00:01:30.227 --> 00:01:32.967
Plan mounting positions that
remain accessible for service.

00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:36.273
After the MOAS has been
installed and brought online,

00:01:36.653 --> 00:01:38.783
the fan interlock we discussed earlier

00:01:38.793 --> 00:01:41.793
prevents operation when
the exhaust fan is off.

00:01:42.393 --> 00:01:45.503
The controller's program
schedule sets the cooking periods

00:01:45.513 --> 00:01:46.833
when treatment is needed.

00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:50.167
Review your cabinet location,
building connections,

00:01:50.407 --> 00:01:54.027
tubing route, and nozzle access
with Molitron before purchasing.

00:01:54.887 --> 00:01:57.667
Agree who will handle
installation and ongoing care,

00:01:57.787 --> 00:01:59.227
then coordinate startup.

00:01:59.907 --> 00:02:01.667
Let's plan the setup for your restaurant.
